WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.750
Speaker 1: I don't know how many of you are
going to believe this or not, but it is very

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.310
true.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:11.070
There is talk of Hillary Clinton 2024.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.610
Let let that sink in.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:20.420
They are talking about Hillary 2024 again,
and what we are seeing is that so far in the

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:29.119
midst of what's going on with COVID and an
understandable frustration with lack of more

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:36.280
tangible accomplishments among many, Joe Biden
and Kamala Harris are being increasingly seen

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:42.890
as uninspiring, unexciting and vulnerable
in 2024.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.399
And I've said before this part, I agree with
completely.

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:52.940
I've said in 2024, if Trump's the nominee
or if DeSantis is the nominee, I don't feel

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:57.269
super confident about Biden versus either
of them.

00:00:57.269 --> 00:01:02.429
And if Biden says I'm not running for reelection,
but here's Kamala, and Kamala is basically

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:07.610
awarded the Democratic nomination, I also
don't feel very confident about that.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:12.130
Some who share my concerns are saying, Let's
look at bringing Hillary back.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.420
The idea being in hindsight, so this is this
is the case some are making.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.780
I'm not making this case.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.190
The case some are making is, listen, the American
public now knows what a mistake it was to

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:24.920
choose Trump over Hillary.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:29.869
So what better way to put a Democrat back
in the White House than to say now do the

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:31.150
right thing with Hillary?

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.110
I think this is potentially disastrous.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:37.509
There is a very interesting article in The
Wall Street Journal, which full disclosure

00:01:37.509 --> 00:01:41.490
The Wall Street Journal is part of News Corp,
Fox News, etc.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:48.340
This is an op ed by Doug Schoen and Andrew
Stein, and it's called Hillary Clinton's 2024

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.340
election comeback.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.880
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris have become unpopular.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.950
It may be time for a change candidate.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.439
Now you can agree with part of this and not
all of it.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:01:58.110
Let me tell you what I mean by that.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:03.670
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris have become unpopular
when you actually look at their average of

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.009
approval ratings.

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:07.509
Joe Biden's actually doing OK.

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:14.440
There is no mathematical case that Joe Biden
is really unpopular, as you can see.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:21.470
Biden's approval came down significantly in
late July through September and into October,

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:27.150
but since then it's basically basically been
steady within one point and it is not unusually

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.150
low.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.820
If you look as FiveThirtyEight allows you
to do.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:36.410
If you look at how Biden compares with past
presidents, Biden is more popular by about

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:43.530
six points at this point in time than Trump
was during his presidency.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.110
And he's sort of close to others.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:51.800
I mean, you know, I think the exception, certainly
with George W. Bush, at this point in time,

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:56.430
Bush had the he was buoyed in his approval
by by nine 11.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:03.400
Joe Biden is less popular right now than Obama,
Clinton, George H.W.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.500
Bush, Reagan, Nixon.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.190
Ford is very, very close and less popular
than Jimmy Carter.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.260
That's true.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.450
But compared to Trump, he's actually doing
better.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:20.620
So for me, the approval rating right now is
not really the signal about whether Joe Biden

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:23.860
can or cannot win in 2024.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:30.401
But what this is a signal about is that there
is no question that it's hard to look at the

00:03:30.401 --> 00:03:34.200
Biden-Harris administration and be excited
now.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.960
To some degree, they were handed a very difficult
situation when it comes to the pandemic.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:43.080
But this is less about popularity today, per
se.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:49.740
It's more about the vision for what do things
look like after the midterms?

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.870
What is it exactly that this administration
is going to stand for or accomplish?

00:03:54.870 --> 00:04:00.010
And to some degree, the reason people are
talking about Hillary is that there aren't

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:05.950
many inspiring figures in the Democratic Party
that people are excited about for 2024.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.260
I know that there is.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.750
Let me go through some of the contingents.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.960
There is a contingent that says it's Bernie's
time.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.290
I believe Bernie's time has come and gone.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:21.100
I don't think a third run from Bernie is going
to be what inspires the Democratic Party to

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:25.270
come together and to defeat whoever is the
Republican in 2024.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.840
I just don't see it, and I know some of you
disagree with me.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:28.930
I love Bernie.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:33.800
I just don't think Bernie at whatever age
he will be.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:38.569
Bernie Sanders age Bernie is 80.

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:47.680
So he would be, what, 80, 82, 82, 83, 83,
84 when he would become.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.801
I just don't see it.

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:50.810
And you can apply the same thing to Biden,
and that's fine.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:51.810
I wouldn't disagree with you.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.720
I think that there's an issue with Biden's
age as well.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.330
I don't think that that's what it is.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:59.009
There's another side that says there's no
one more exciting than AOC.

00:04:59.009 --> 00:05:03.539
I think it would be really tough in 24 for
AOC to run for president.

00:05:03.539 --> 00:05:05.300
Would she even be old enough?

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.300
That's another question.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:13.520
When will AOC be old enough to run for president?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:19.740
She turns 35 a few weeks before Election Day,
OK, so she may be eligible.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:26.169
I have a really hard time imagining that AOC
is going to win the presidency in 2024, despite

00:05:26.169 --> 00:05:28.380
a lot of people being very excited about her.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:33.210
So then you end up with people saying stuff,
Well, what about Warren Boudette, judge?

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:37.930
And it makes a lot of progressives cringe,
even though when you look on paper, Warren's

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:43.259
one of the few people proposing a wealth tax,
something very popular with the progressives.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:49.190
Boudette judge is one of the few guys who
can actually consistently out rhetoric, whoever

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:54.139
it is he's talking about, Fox News host whatever,
but it doesn't feel like it's going to really

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:57.790
inspire the widest swath of the Democratic
Party.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.960
So I get why people are again saying, I don't
know.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.530
Maybe Hillary again, she's younger than some
of these other people, but it strikes me as

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.639
potentially disastrous.

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:09.900
Let me know your thoughts.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.789
You can find me on Twitter at Packman.

00:06:11.789 --> 00:07:18.750
We'll take a break and be back right after
this.

